      "id": "ig-sound-vowel-harmony",
      "title": "Vowel harmony and dotted vowels",
      "steps": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "duration_seconds": 22,
          "body_en": "Standard Igbo spelling uses dotted vowels ị, ọ, and ụ plus ṅ (assets/data/keyboard/layouts.json, ig; CURRICULUM.md#§3.3:L525). Igbo also has vowel harmony: affix vowels match the harmonic class of nearby stem vowels (ELEVATION.md#§11.2:L1789; register:fsi-igbo). Pedagogical tone marks stay kit-defined — this tutorial does not teach tone labels.",
          "source_ids": [
            "assets/data/keyboard/layouts.json#ig",
            "CURRICULUM.md#§3.3:L525",
            "ELEVATION.md#§11.2:L1789",
            "register:fsi-igbo"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "duration_seconds": 26,
          "body_en": "Notice dotted vowels in cited A1 lemmas ahịa (market) and ụlọ (house), then listen for the harmonizing perfect suffix in O gụrụ akwụkwọ (completed reading) from the progressive pattern contrasts (assets/data/patterns/ig.json#ig.pat.progressive-na). Native mouth video fills in after EXT-13 capture (P7-933).",
